id: pm-oybmsd
title: Align SDK producer-continuation result types with sparse reference envelopes
description: "During default-list acceptance, native PmClient.list({brief:true,limit:'1',after:cursor}) returns a sparse reference envelope ending with next_cursor:null; fields such as has_more and sorting are intentionally absent. ListResultBase and ListVerboseResult still require those fields, and PmReadOutputResultFor considers budget/session/outputCursor but not producer after options. Audit the public return-type contract against the advertised continuation envelope before choosing a fix; preserve the intentional runtime metadata-reference optimization."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[3]: pagination,sdk,types
created_at: "2026-10-20T07:43:13.561Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-21T05:41:23.656Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-21T05:41:21.784Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-21T05:41:21.784Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: Type fixtures reflect first-page and producer-continuation envelopes without promising absent fields; CLI SDK and MCP serialized continuations retain complete membership and sparse metadata; public surface compatibility and packed consumer checks pass
parent: pm-srns
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Native SDK producer continuations now expose optional repeated metadata and a typed reference contract derived from the runtime suppression keys. No-cursor reads and low-level producer contracts remain intact, including optional and generic-record cursor inputs."
expected_result: "SDK callers handle sparse continuation metadata safely while native, CLI and MCP membership and packed Node/Bun behavior remain correct."
actual_result: "All four TypeScript configurations, final linked checks, source negative controls and packed public declaration consumers pass. Complete accepted coverage passes 10922 tests with 3 configured skips across 841 files and exact lines 66427/66427, statements 70072/70072, functions 14436/14436 and branches 53858/53858. Initial failed receipts are preserved; required hosted review and CI remain merge admission."
